rl Weber"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/DEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/DEN.png"}] "DEN"]]] [:tr {:class "hidden_referees", :style "display: none"} [:th {} "Judge / Referee"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5002629"} "Juan Casanovas"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ESP"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ESP.png"}] "ESP"]]] [:tr {:class "hidden_referees", :style "display: none"} [:th {} "Judge / Referee"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5002469"} "Henri Babig"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/LUX"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/LUX.png"}] "LUX"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/7998"} "Willie Smith"] " of South Africa, like flyweight champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/8710"} "Fidel LaBarba"] ", was a mere 19 years old when he became Olympic champion. Smith, who learned boxing at the orphanage where he was raised, fought with a cautious approach to outpoint " [:a {:href "/athletes/8789"} "Al Tripoli"] " of the USA in the final. As a professional, he went to win a version of the World bantamweight title. Frenchman " [:a {:href "/athletes/3010"} "Jean Ces"] "’ bronze medal was the only boxing medal won by the host nation in 1924."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Of the 20 bouts contested in the division, all but one were decided by judges’ decision.  The American " [:a {:href "/athletes/8716"} "Joseph Lazarus"] " was the unlucky victim of disqualification in his bout against " [:a {:href "/athletes/8137"} "Oscar Andrén"] " of Sweden. The Swede was knocked out, but the referee, Sigel of France, ruled Lazarus had struck his opponent illegally, disobeying instructions to step back from a clinch. Sigel would later apologize to US team officials for his mistaken decision but, despite the urging of Andrén and Swedish team officials, no appeal was made."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/7998"} "Willie Smith"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RSA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/RSA.png"}] "RSA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/8789"} "Al Tripoli"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/3010"} "Jean Ces"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/8137"} "Oscar Andrén"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/2886"} "Antonio Sánchez"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ESP"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ESP.png"}] "ESP"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/3358"} "Alf Barber"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "paddi